{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Separated the two halves of the sweep account and corrected the liveness half. The safety half stands on CheckRun 35a6c1074291424686f0360747f6c268 index 16 (seeds=60, steps_per_seed=60, elections=466, ordinary proposals=452, conf_change_proposals=249, restarts=471, violations=0): no witness appeared for at-most-one-leader-per-term, committed (index, term) consistency, committed-index monotonicity or applied <= committed across configuration changes (half of them joint with the target's own auto-leave), restarts rebuilt from persisted hard state and applied ConfState, and ordinary traffic. The liveness half does not stand: the antecedent counter reports unapplied_conf_change_states=0 for the same revision because the sweep applies every node to its committed index on every step, so no check point ever presented the conjunction the witness counts, which makes stalled_states=0 uninterpretable in both directions. I withdrew my earlier sentence that the guard's suppression never coincided with a configuration lacking a promotable node, since it was an artifact of the event mix rather than an observation about the target, and re-scoped the investigation's defect claim from refuted to unresolved: what remains is a necessary measurement - the harness must let application fall behind (apply a subset of nodes, or skip the apply step for a chosen node) before the guard's bounded-liveness cost can be assessed, and the receipt for any such run would have to show the antecedent counter non-zero before a stalled_states value means anything. The new interpretation cites the recorded knowledge entry, keeps the inherited limitations of the safety half (between-events checks, term rather than full-identity comparison, no storage faults, no demotion of an existing serving voter), and no experiment was requested because the event that makes the measurement non-vacuous is still to be built.\"}"}}
